<%# SLA Met card for the SLA Trend tab — the one date-scoped figure on the dashboard. @window_counts %>
<%# is computed over tickets RESOLVED inside the selected window (Sla::DashboardScope resolved_range), %>
<%# kept separate from the always-current @counts so the Open Tickets tab is never affected by the %>
<%# date range. Closed-loop compliance: open tickets never appear here, because an open ticket has %>
<%# not yet met anything. %>
<%# Denominator is Counts#evaluated (met + breached), NOT total — a No-SLA ticket resolved in the %>
<%# window was never evaluated and must not drag the percentage down. %>
<%# %>
<%# Same _summary_card anatomy as the Open Tickets tab's row (icon tile, label, big number, muted %>
<%# caption) so the two tabs share one card design and one type scale. The surface is overridden to %>
<%# white: this card stands alone beside the chart rather than in a row of five, where the tinted %>
<%# fills exist to tell the five states apart at a glance. %>
<%= render 'sla_dashboard/summary_card',
      state: :met, label: sla_card_label(:met_window),
      surface: 'tw-bg-white tw-border-gray-200',
      value: safe_join([
        content_tag(:span, sla_percentage(@window_counts.met, @window_counts.evaluated), id: 'sla-met-window-percentage'),
        '%'
      ]),
      caption: l(:text_sla_met_in_target, met: @window_counts.met, total: @window_counts.evaluated) %>
